<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Li of Zhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 877–841 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Li of Zhou was the tenth king of the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>, reigning from about 877 to 841 BCE. His harsh rule, monopolies and suppression of criticism provoked a revolt in the capital in 841 BCE, which drove him into exile at Zhi. The Gonghe regency that followed began the first securely dated year of Chinese history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-li-of-zhou.jpg" alt="King Li of Zhou" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 幽灵巴尼 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hu_Gui_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
